%% Phase coupling analysis between thalamic spindles and neuronal spikes
% This script analyzes the phase relationship between thalamic spindle
% activity and neuronal spiking across multiple recording sessions. For
% each neuron, the script identifies its corresponding reference channel
% and extracts the instantaneous phase of the thalamic signal using the
% Hilbert transform. Spike phases are then obtained around spindle events
% using a ±0.25-s time window.
%
% Spindle events are separated into global and local spindles based on the
% previously classified spindle populations. The phase distributions of
% spikes occurring around all spindles, global spindles, and local spindles
% are independently extracted and tested for non-uniformity using the
% circular Rayleigh test. Neurons showing significant phase locking
% (p < 0.05) are counted and their mean preferred phases are calculated.
%
% Circular histograms are generated for significantly coupled neurons,
% together with the corresponding mean phase and statistical significance.
% Finally, the mean phase distributions across all analyzed neurons are
% evaluated separately for all, global, and local spindle events. The
% resulting figures are saved in both PNG and MATLAB FIG formats for
% subsequent visualization and analysis.


